Bridge 0130: Turnip reads center varyings as they are, no InterpolateAtOffset(0). In a multisampled pipeline every
center-sampled float varying was read through GLSL.std.450 InterpolateAtOffset at offset 0 (Source::PixelCenter)
unless the device had VkProperty::MetalCenterVaryings (MoltenVK only); ir3 lowers that to ddx/ddy with helper
invocations live (games_fps hot WebGL shader: 12 derivatives, 466/1249 instructions with helpers). Mesa facts:
an undecorated input loads load_barycentric_pixel (nir_lower_io.c:354-360), the same pixel-center ij ir3's
InterpolateAtOffset starts from (ir3_nir_lower_load_barycentric_at_offset.c:24-25), also when a SampleId read
turns the shader per-sample (spirv_to_nir.c:8051-8054 sets uses_sample_shading only; freedreno never calls
nir_lower_sample_shading). But sampleShadingEnable sets force_sample_interp (tu_pipeline.cc:1947-1948), which
decorates every non-centroid input Sample (tu_shader.cc:3287-3292). So Turnip (VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_TURNIP) gets
MetalCenterVaryings plus DriverWorkaround::SampleShadingMovesCenterVaryings; with the latter a function that may
write memory (the AIR side-effect walk of lower::fragment::discard, a superset of StageInterface::writes_memory,
under which link enables sample shading) keeps InterpolateAtOffset(0). The profile fingerprint hashes both, so
cached artifacts of the old path are not reused; the codec already encodes the property. Upstream metal2vulkan
(origin f6a96b7d) only has MoltenVK rows (1.4.1, 1.4.2) for this fact; nothing to reuse.
Logs `SWEET_M2V_CENTER_VARY mode N` once per process (with SWEET_PIPESTATS).
Knob: SWEET_M2V_CENTER_VARY (default 1; 0 = InterpolateAtOffset(0) as before).

